{
  "id": "uniqueness",
  "term": "uniqueness",
  "definition": "In visual statistical learning, uniqueness refers to how specifically one stimulus predicts another, taking into account not just how often the outcome follows the cue but also how exclusively they are linked to each other. It describes the distinctiveness of a predictive relationship rather than simple co-occurrence alone.",
